        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\", Sweet Charity\n- People: Cy Coleman, Dorothy Fields, Neil Simon, Bob Fosse, Gwen Verdon, John McMartin\n- Roles: Vittorio, Charity\n\nFacts:\n- \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\" is a song from the 1966 Broadway musical Sweet Charity.\n- Cy Coleman wrote the music for Sweet Charity, Dorothy Fields wrote the lyrics, and Neil Simon wrote the book.\n- Bob Fosse directed and choreographed Sweet Charity for Broadway.\n- Gwen Verdon, Bob Fosse's wife and muse, starred in Sweet Charity alongside John McMartin.\n- In \"If My Friends Could See Me Now,\" the character Charity reflects on her marvelous luck while spending time with the fortune teller Vittorio.",
