        "original_id": "25fec36e-9874-5655-81e2-2bd7686d53f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\"\n- Musicals and Films: \"Sweet Charity\"\n- People: Cy Coleman, Dorothy Fields, Gwen Verdon, Shirley MacLaine, Bob Fosse, John McMartin, Vittorio, Charity\n\nFacts:\n- \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\" is a song from the 1966 Broadway musical \"Sweet Charity\".\n- Cy Coleman wrote the music for \"If My Friends Could See Me Now,\" and Dorothy Fields wrote its lyrics.\n- In \"Sweet Charity,\" the character Charity reflects on her good luck while spending time with Vittorio.\n- Gwen Verdon played Charity in the original New York cast of \"Sweet Charity.\"\n- Bob Fosse directed and choreographed the Broadway production of \"Sweet Charity.\"\n- Gwen Verdon and John McMartin starred in the Broadway production of \"Sweet Charity.\"\n- In the 1969 film adaptation of \"Sweet Charity,\" Shirley MacLaine performed \"If My Friends Could See Me Now.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
